###Pure
// H3 (b), SCRATCH (the compatibility homework, 2026-11-19): legend-pure's toString, written as a LITE program, for the
// PURE input adapter to call in place of upstream's name. A Float prints as legend-pure prints it -- the one named
// core capability meta::legend::lite::pureFloatText (CompiledSupport.primitiveToString: DecimalFormat "0.0", up to 340
// fraction digits, zero as 0.0); any other value prints as lite's own toString, which is legend-pure's already.

function meta::legend::compat::pure::toString(f: Float[1]): String[1]
{
    meta::legend::lite::pureFloatText($f)
}

function meta::legend::compat::pure::toString(a: Any[1]): String[1]
{
    meta::pure::functions::string::toString($a)
}
